WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.836
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The tonight Show," everyone.

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:06.039
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.273
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:08.541
Well, let's get to some news.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:10.110 line:0%
Guys, President Biden
is wrapping up

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.778 line:0%
his first trip to Asia
since taking office

00:00:12.778 --> 00:00:16.216 line:0%
after spending a few days
in South Korea and Japan.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:17.883
So, if you're keeping track,

00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:21.087
there's a drought out West,
inflation is still headed north,

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.422
Biden's in the Far East,

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.858
and his approval rating
is down south.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.593
But Biden's trip is going well.

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:29.662
So far, he's only made one
statement that The White House

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:32.331
had to immediately walk back.

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:34.333
Biden spent the weekend
in South Korea,

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.101
and you could tell he really
started to pick up on

00:00:36.101 --> 00:00:37.136
South Korean culture.

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:38.137
Watch this.

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:42.308
♪♪

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:43.877
-Smooth like butter.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:46.045
Like a criminal under cover.

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.113
Gonna pop like trouble.

00:00:48.113 --> 00:00:49.848
Breaking into your
heart like that.

00:00:49.848 --> 00:00:50.950
-Yeah.
[ Cash register dings ]

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.820
Not bad.
He was just getting into it.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.221
-Yeah.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.425
-Of course, a big focus of
Biden's trip

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.361
to Asia is the threat of
North Korea.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:02.928 line:0%
And yesterday,
when a reporter asked Biden

00:01:02.928 --> 00:01:05.665 line:0%
if he had a message for
Kim Jong-un, he said,

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.634 line:0%
"Hello. Period."

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.669
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.872
That sounds like a grandpa
trying to send a voice text.

00:01:13.872 --> 00:01:17.276
Like, "Hello. Period.

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:19.546
Happy birthday. Stop."

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.116
Yep, Biden said he's open to
meeting with Kim Jong-un

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:26.352
if Kim is "sincere and serious."

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:29.122
And Kim was like, "Oh, I think
I gave you the wrong idea.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:32.058
I'm just looking to have
fun hookups this summer."

00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:34.393
Yep, sincere and serious.

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:36.429
That sounds like a
"Fast and the Furious" spin-off

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.331
for your mom.

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:41.300
Meanwhile, North Korea could be
resuming nuclear tests

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.302
for the first time
in nearly five years.

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:45.638
But Biden said
he's not concerned.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:47.340
Yep. That's how things are
going right now.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.541
North Korea is launching a nuke,

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.609
and it's like eighth on
Biden's to-do list.

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:52.044
He's like, "Yeah, okay."

00:01:52.044 --> 00:01:53.279
Yep, on his trip to Asia,

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.381
Biden has talked about
a wide range of issues.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.616
And I thought he had some pretty
interesting things to say.

00:01:57.616 --> 00:01:58.685
Here's Biden at a meeting.

00:02:14.099 --> 00:02:17.536 line:0%
Interesting. I just -- I don't
know what he's talk--

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:20.005
-Wow!
-It's just interesting.

00:02:20.005 --> 00:02:22.442
Next, here he is at a dinner.
Listen to this.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:39.325
I just...

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:40.726
It's just interesting,
what he says.

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:43.329
-Licorice soda.
-Wow.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.363
-Here he is touring
a Samsung factory.

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:45.431
Listen to this.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.113
It's just interesting.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:05.051 line:0%
Well, switching gears,
today, Starbucks

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.720 line:0%
announced that after 15 years
in business,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.423 line:0%
they're closing down all 130
of their cafés in Russia

00:03:11.423 --> 00:03:12.992 line:0%
and leaving permanently.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.326
That's a tough break
for Russians,

00:03:14.326 --> 00:03:15.995
because they were just a month
away from their favorite

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:18.330
coffee release,
the Putin-spiced latte.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.800
Yeah. Well, some business news.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.002
I read that Applebee's
doesn't want its restaurants

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:25.571
taking pickup orders
over the phone anymore.

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:28.507
So it's setting up call centers
to do it for them.

00:03:28.507 --> 00:03:29.675
Actually,
there's several restaurants

00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:31.243
that use call centers,
and each one

00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:33.412
has a very unique greeting
when you call.

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:35.114
For example,
here's the Applebee's greeting.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:39.986
Yeah, pretty standard stuff.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.555
Then here's Benihana's greeting.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.600
-Wow!

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.804
-Next, here's the greeting from
Tommy Bahama.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:08.414
-♪ Are you reelin'
in the years ♪

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:09.682
♪ Stowin' away the time ♪

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.217
-Yeah, it's pretty good.

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:14.921
And, finally, here's the
greeting for Chuck E. Cheese.

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:15.989
-Chuck E. Cheese.
-Yeah.

00:04:20.025 --> 00:04:21.793
Interesting. Wow.

00:04:21.793 --> 00:04:23.429
They're all different.

00:04:25.731 --> 00:04:26.865
Well, get this.

00:04:26.865 --> 00:04:28.501 line:0%
I saw that Hot Pockets
is coming out with

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:31.637 line:0%
a new thaw-and-eat sandwich.

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:33.539 line:0%
So instead of using
the microwave,

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:34.940 line:0%
you just take it
out of the freezer

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.442 line:0%
and let it sit for a few hours.

00:04:38.677 --> 00:04:40.580
Mmm!

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:44.083
Nothing more delicious than
a room-temperature pocket.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.084
You can't win with Hot Pockets.

00:04:46.084 --> 00:04:48.087
You either have to wait
three hours for them to cool off

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.390
or three hours
for them to heat up.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.958
Oh, I heard --
Guys, check this out.

00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:54.326
I heard that authorities
in the Midwest

00:04:54.326 --> 00:04:57.129
are on the lookout for TikTokers
who have damaged property

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:59.899
while doing something called the
Kool-Aid Man Challenge.

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:00.967
Take a look at this.

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:03.035 line:0%
-It's called the
Kool-Aid Man Challenge,

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:05.604 line:0%
and it's recently gone viral
in Nebraska.

00:05:05.604 --> 00:05:07.973 line:0%
Teens are running
into fences, saying,

00:05:07.973 --> 00:05:10.243 line:0%
"Oh, yeah!"
like the Kool-Aid Man

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:11.711 line:0%
and knocking the fence down.

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:14.046
-Yeah.

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:15.314
It's pretty serious.

00:05:15.314 --> 00:05:18.251
So here now via satellite to
discuss the trend is

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:20.619
the guy who started it all,
Kool-Aid Man.

00:05:20.619 --> 00:05:23.055
Kool-Aid Man, are you there?
-Oh, yeah!

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:25.391
-Alright.
Thank you for being here.

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.859
Do you use TikTok?

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:29.095
-Oh, yeah!

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:31.029
-And so you've seen
the Kool-Aid Man challenge.

00:05:31.029 --> 00:05:32.865
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.199
-So you agree it's dangerous.

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:36.002
-Oh, yeah!

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.570
-Do you think the people
who have knocked down fences

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:38.738
should have to pay for them?

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:41.307
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:42.808
Is that all you
have to say about it?

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:44.743
-Oh, yeah!

00:05:44.743 --> 00:05:46.278
-I guess you have
to be careful of what you say,

00:05:46.278 --> 00:05:47.747
in case anyone
decides to sue you.

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:49.348
-Oh, yeah!
-Yeah, alright.

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:51.083
Hey, real quick, before you go,
I always wanted to know this.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:52.918
What kind of Kool-Aid
is in your pitcher?

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:55.088
-It's actually my blood, Jimmy.

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:57.056
I'm just a pitcher of blood.

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:59.925
But when you think about it,
aren't we all?

00:05:59.925 --> 00:06:01.327
-Kool-Aid Man, everyone.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:03.363
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:07.199
Hey, did you guys
hear about this?

00:06:07.199 --> 00:06:08.934
Jif peanut butter
is being recalled

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:11.203
